       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum daily dose for metformin (generally 2550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2000 mg/day for extended-release). At that dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is serious, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a transcription error. A common possibility is 850 mg or 1000 mg three times daily, but I can't determine the intended dose.\n\nPlease have a licensed prescriber review and confirm the dose before any order is placed. If they confirm a dose, they or a clinician on the team can submit it through the order-entry system, or send me the confirmed dose and formulation and I can enter it."
