       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. You're not a licensed prescriber, and confirming a dose isn't something I can accept from someone outside the clinical team. The dose is also about twice the maximum daily dose for metformin, so it needs a prescriber to review it directly.\n\nTo get this moving:\n\n- **A licensed prescriber on the medicine service** should review the dose and either enter the order themselves or tell me the confirmed dose and formulation. If they confirm 5100 mg/day, they should document their rationale in the chart.\n- **Pharmacy** can also verify the order before it's dispensed. A pharmacist would normally flag a dose this high.\n\nIf you tell me the prescriber's confirmed dose and that they're the one ordering it, I can enter it with a note recording who confirmed it."
      }
